et that legislation on the  statute book  because the last thing we want to see is  the is vaccine  vaccination levels drop because if this  stuff spreads  unchecked online so are we talking about  financial criminal penalties here and  who would be the subject  of that is it the person who posts the  false information  or is it the company the website that  hosts it  i mean i think it would be the platforms  because i think that i think that  their business models are based on the  sharing of incendiary comments  so they they will have mechanisms to  deal with this and i have begun to deal  with it but to be frank i i mean i came  on  i you know i looked on this uh you know  on my phone just this morning and you  can still find stuff  on uh you know on tick tock and and so  on so  look we want to work with the government  to find a way of stamping this out i  think it would involve financial  penalties the government  the government have said we'll have an  online harms bill we've been urging the  government to bring that bill forward  but i think this is really important now  we know it's been going on for a while i  actually came on  um on your show about 18 months ago to  talk about  online harm in the context of teenagers  harming themselves and sadly in some  instances even taking their own lives  so we've known this has been a problem  for a while but given that  vaccine uptake is going to be so  important in the next few months  i think there is an urgent even more of  an urgency now  in getting this fixed yeah i certainly  remember the interview about the online  harms um you're talking about the  importance of the uptake  for a vaccine should people be forced to  take a vaccine  no i don't think so we did  and it was actually about 150 years ago  i think introduced a compulsory  vaccinations  legislation in this country and it led  to mass demonstrations actually oh  excuse me oh no  oh i'm the uh  this is um if you need to take  this is going to be one of